Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fca36d54-5515-c847-b124-36ab028f5c2c"],

Cell["\<\
1. Minimum Pulse Duration: In Lab 1A, lower the duration from 10 ms toward 2 \
ms at RF limit 120 Hz for Universal pi/2_x versus State Inversion. Where does \
each hit the quantum speed limit?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7fb09823-cd72-c541-b95f-e44aa5f250ec"],

Cell["\<\
2. Discretisation coarseness: Drop Nt from 30 to 10 slices at +150 Hz offset \
and inspect whether 10 piecewise-constant slices still afford enough degrees \
of freedom.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"be58708e-aac3-8642-9a2c-257257669b23"],

Cell["\<\
3. Amplitude vs Duration trade-off: Reduce RF Disk Limit from 120 Hz to 50 Hz \
at 10 ms duration and compare Cartesian vs AmplitudePhase waveforms.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d8d4e14b-9933-c843-b289-9c9b2dc2a023"],

Cell["\<\
4. Bandwidth sensitivity: In Lab 1B, shift Test Offset from +50 Hz to 0 Hz or \
+150 Hz; observe why a pulse optimised at a single offset fails away from 50 \
Hz (motivating Notebook 05).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9c2de040-3d26-864e-a21f-f5a7f7c2ffc9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"45f0eef7-5aa2-b24f-88ec-b2c7b0afaafd"],

Cell["\<\
We demonstrated single-spin inversion and universal pi/2_x synthesis in Hz \
units, verified propagator equivalence with SpinDynamica's \
NPropagationOperator, and contrasted point-to-point state transfer against \
full unitary gates. Using queued evaluation buttons for GRAPE optimisations \
paired with instant forward propagation enables rapid interactive exploration \
without FrontEnd freezes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b0df21f0-2409-0d48-a77c-613518ac404b"],

